{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b140254bd361fcd7","name":"card_unit_8th_marines","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_8th_marines","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"8th MARINES","text":"Deployment: Deal 1 damage to adjacent units. They get +2 attack.","flavorText":"The 8th Marine Regiment played a significant role during WWII as part of the United States Marine Corps. The regiment was initially formed in 1917 but was disbanded after WWI. It was reactivated in 1940 and deployed to various theaters in the Pacific.After extensive jungle training the regiment began their wartime service by defending the Samoan Islands. They later sailed to Guadalcanal to reinforce the 1st Marine Division engaged in the grueling Battle of Guadalcanal. It was during this campaign that the regiment earned its first Presidential Unit Citation for its bravery and achievements. Following their time in Guadalcanal, the 8th Marines joined the 2nd Marine Division in New Zealand, where they prepared for the Battle of Tarawa. During the battle, the regiment played a vital role in capturing the island, which opened the door to the Japanese Empire. For their actions in Tarawa, the 8th Marine Regiment was awarded their second Presidential Unit Citation. After refitting in Hawaii, the regiment participated in the Marianas campaign, storming the beaches of Saipan and Tinian. These victories provided key bases for launching air attacks against Japan. Finally, the 8th Marines joined the 1st and 6th Marine Divisions in the Battle of Okinawa, where they faced fierce Japanese resistance. The regiment's involvement in Okinawa marked the last major battle of WWII.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":6,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_8th_marines","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_8th_marines_title","SourceString":"8th MARINES","LocalizedString":"8th MARINES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":6,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_8th_marines_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Deal 1 damage to adjacent units. They get +2 attack.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Deal 1 damage to adjacent units. They get +2 attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_8th_marines_history","SourceString":"The 8th Marine Regiment played a significant role during WWII as part of the United States Marine Corps. The regiment was initially formed in 1917 but was disbanded after WWI. It was reactivated in 1940 and deployed to various theaters in the Pacific.After extensive jungle training the regiment began their wartime service by defending the Samoan Islands. They later sailed to Guadalcanal to reinforce the 1st Marine Division engaged in the grueling Battle of Guadalcanal. It was during this campaign that the regiment earned its first Presidential Unit Citation for its bravery and achievements. Following their time in Guadalcanal, the 8th Marines joined the 2nd Marine Division in New Zealand, where they prepared for the Battle of Tarawa. During the battle, the regiment played a vital role in capturing the island, which opened the door to the Japanese Empire. For their actions in Tarawa, the 8th Marine Regiment was awarded their second Presidential Unit Citation. After refitting in Hawaii, the regiment participated in the Marianas campaign, storming the beaches of Saipan and Tinian. These victories provided key bases for launching air attacks against Japan. Finally, the 8th Marines joined the 1st and 6th Marine Divisions in the Battle of Okinawa, where they faced fierce Japanese resistance. The regiment's involvement in Okinawa marked the last major battle of WWII.","LocalizedString":"The 8th Marine Regiment played a significant role during WWII as part of the United States Marine Corps. The regiment was initially formed in 1917 but was disbanded after WWI. It was reactivated in 1940 and deployed to various theaters in the Pacific.After extensive jungle training the regiment began their wartime service by defending the Samoan Islands. They later sailed to Guadalcanal to reinforce the 1st Marine Division engaged in the grueling Battle of Guadalcanal. It was during this campaign that the regiment earned its first Presidential Unit Citation for its bravery and achievements. Following their time in Guadalcanal, the 8th Marines joined the 2nd Marine Division in New Zealand, where they prepared for the Battle of Tarawa. During the battle, the regiment played a vital role in capturing the island, which opened the door to the Japanese Empire. For their actions in Tarawa, the 8th Marine Regiment was awarded their second Presidential Unit Citation. After refitting in Hawaii, the regiment participated in the Marianas campaign, storming the beaches of Saipan and Tinian. These victories provided key bases for launching air attacks against Japan. Finally, the 8th Marines joined the 1st and 6th Marine Divisions in the Battle of Okinawa, where they faced fierce Japanese resistance. The regiment's involvement in Okinawa marked the last major battle of WWII."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"hasDeployment":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Medium'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Medium.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/Spring2023Candidates/t_marines_or_some.t_marines_or_some","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/8th_MARINES.8th_MARINES","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":480.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_8th_marines_photo","SourceString":"US Marines during the Battle of Saipan,1944.","LocalizedString":"US Marines during the B